Drop the libxklavier dependency.

liblightdm-gobject links libxklavier for one thing: enumerating the keyboard
layouts the X server knows about, so a greeter can offer a layout menu.
libxklavier is not ported -- it would bring in iso-codes and its own XKB
registry parser -- and Tunix has a single layout, set in /etc/vconsole.conf and
applied by the X server, that nothing in a greeter could change anyway.

So the list is empty and there is no current layout. The LightDMLayout GObject
is deliberately left alone: it is public API, and lightdm-gtk-greeter builds a
menu from it whether or not it has any rows.

